    "enUS": {
      "description": "The Midsummer Fire Festival is celebrated everywhere in Azeroth, and the diverse land of Kalimdor is no exception. You look fit to travel -- perhaps a journey is in order.\n\nMidsummer cannot be truly appreciated unless you've seen the blistering blue fires abroad. The celebrants have lit fires in chilly western Winterspring, northeastern Azshara, near Valor's Rest in the wastes of Silithus, and by the entrance to lush Un'Goro. Return once your journey is complete.",
      "objectiveLines": [
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "{current}/{required} Flame of Azshara",
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "{current}/{required} Flame of Silithus",
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "{current}/{required} Flame of Un'Goro",
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "text": "{current}/{required} Flame of Winterspring",
          "type": "object"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "Visit the Midsummer camps located in Azshara, Silithus, Un'Goro Crater, and Winterspring, then return to the Festival Flamekeeper.",
      "title": "Wild Fires in Kalimdor",
